1
00:00:01,939 --> 00:00:10,600
Welcome to Brazil's states, part 2 of 2. First, I clear the chosen names for a
fresh regional lesson.

2
00:00:11,259 --> 00:00:21,754
We work through 13 of the Brazil regions the map names, once each: where it
sits, one fact worth keeping, and a hook to remember it by.

3
00:00:22,434 --> 00:00:24,779
Let's bring Rondônia into view.

4
00:00:32,581 --> 00:00:44,052
Rondônia sits in the far west, inland along the Madeira and Guaporé rivers,
with Porto Velho, its largest city, on the Madeira and Acre, Amazonas and Mato
Grosso to its north and east.

5
00:00:44,706 --> 00:00:55,201
The Madeira-Mamoré railway built here cost thousands of lives to malaria and
was abandoned, and the state later became a front line of Amazon
deforestation.

6
00:00:55,853 --> 00:01:04,932
Remember the railway that was abandoned to malaria, and the western state that
became a front line of clearing the Amazon.

7
00:01:05,671 --> 00:01:08,179
Let's bring Mato Grosso into view.

8
00:01:14,161 --> 00:01:27,338
Mato Grosso fills the centre of Brazil, from the Amazon forest down to the
Pantanal, with Cuiabá, its largest city, in its southern half and Pará,
Tocantins and Rondônia to its north.

9
00:01:28,003 --> 00:01:36,316
Its southern half holds the Pantanal, the largest tropical wetland in the
world and the best place on earth to see a wild jaguar.

10
00:01:36,966 --> 00:01:45,453
Remember the wetland where jaguars swim in its south and the soy frontier
racing into the forest in its north.

11
00:01:46,135 --> 00:01:48,097
Let's bring Bahia into view.

12
00:01:52,985 --> 00:02:04,502
Bahia occupies the east coast around the great bay of All Saints, with
Salvador, its largest city, on the shore and its land reaching inland to Goiás
and Tocantins.

13
00:02:05,152 --> 00:02:14,052
Salvador was the capital of Brazil until 1763 and received more enslaved
Africans than any other port in the Americas.

14
00:02:14,701 --> 00:02:22,375
Remember the bay of All Saints and the old capital, where the berimbau,
capoeira and candomblé all belong.

15
00:02:23,083 --> 00:02:25,556
Let's bring Distrito Federal into view.

16
00:02:31,636 --> 00:02:42,166
The Distrito Federal is the federal district, not a state in the ordinary
sense, cut out of the middle of the country, with Brasília inside it and Goiás
and Minas Gerais around it.

17
00:02:42,829 --> 00:03:02,557
Brasília was built in 41 months and inaugurated in 1960, designed by Lúcio
Costa and Oscar Niemeyer in the shape of an aeroplane or a bird, and it is the
only city built in the twentieth century to be a UNESCO World Heritage site.

18
00:03:03,222 --> 00:03:11,662
Remember the district that is not a state, holding the capital built from
scratch in forty-one months in the middle of the country.

19
00:03:12,347 --> 00:03:14,599
Let's bring Goiás into view.

20
00:03:19,123 --> 00:03:32,602
Goiás lies in the centre of Brazil, with Goiânia, its largest city, in the
middle, the Distrito Federal cut into its eastern heart and Minas Gerais, Mato
Grosso, Tocantins and Bahia around it.

21
00:03:33,260 --> 00:03:41,700
Gold was found here in 1722, and the colonial centre of Goiás Velho survives
from that rush as a UNESCO site.

22
00:03:42,350 --> 00:03:49,595
Remember the gold rush that made the state, and the high plateau of quartz and
waterfalls in its north-east.

23
00:03:50,304 --> 00:03:52,429
Let's bring Minas Gerais into view.

24
00:03:59,717 --> 00:04:12,848
Minas Gerais lies inland in the south-east, between Bahia and São Paulo, with
Belo Horizonte, its largest city, in its middle and the Atlantic coast of Rio
de Janeiro and Espírito Santo beyond it.

25
00:04:13,500 --> 00:04:25,737
So much gold was dug here that the crown took a fifth, and the tax revolt
against it in 1789, the Inconfidência Mineira, is the founding story of
Brazilian independence.

26
00:04:26,389 --> 00:04:35,259
Remember the general mines of gold and diamonds, and Ouro Preto’s churches
carved by a sculptor whose hands were strapped to his tools.

27
00:04:35,954 --> 00:04:39,228
Let's bring Espírito Santo into view.

28
00:04:45,390 --> 00:04:57,418
Espírito Santo is a narrow coastal state in the south-east, with Vitória, its
largest city, on the shore and Bahia, Minas Gerais and Rio de Janeiro around
it.

29
00:04:58,081 --> 00:05:06,475
It was named Holy Spirit on Pentecost in 1535, and it is Brazil’s largest
producer of robusta coffee.

30
00:05:07,130 --> 00:05:17,196
Remember the Atlantic coffee state, with its Italian-descended rural families
and the granite dome at Pedra Azul that changes colour through the day.

31
00:05:17,880 --> 00:05:21,026
Let's bring Mato Grosso do Sul into view.

32
00:05:28,263 --> 00:05:40,117
Mato Grosso do Sul is the southern half of Mato Grosso in the centre-west,
with Campo Grande, its largest city, inside it and Paraguay and Bolivia along
its western side.

33
00:05:40,771 --> 00:05:51,220
Bonito in it has rivers so clear you can snorkel them and see forty metres to
the bottom, kept that way by limestone filtering the water.

34
00:05:51,879 --> 00:06:02,328
Remember the rivers at Bonito clear enough to snorkel, and the southern
Pantanal that is flooded for half the year and grazed for the other half.

35
00:06:03,025 --> 00:06:05,324
Let's bring Rio de Janeiro into view.

36
00:06:10,480 --> 00:06:22,763
Rio de Janeiro lies on the south-east coast, with its capital city of the same
name on Guanabara Bay, Minas Gerais behind it and Espírito Santo and São Paulo
beside it.

37
00:06:23,422 --> 00:06:35,531
Portuguese sailors entered Guanabara Bay on the first of January 1502 and took
it for a river mouth, which is where the state gets its name.

38
00:06:36,193 --> 00:06:43,693
Remember the January river that is really a bay, with Christ the Redeemer
above it and the biggest carnival on earth below.

39
00:06:44,562 --> 00:06:46,687
Let's bring São Paulo into view.

40
00:06:54,003 --> 00:07:05,474
São Paulo fills the south-east of Brazil, touching the Atlantic to the east,
with the city of São Paulo, the largest in the southern hemisphere, in its
eastern half and Paraná to the south.

41
00:07:06,132 --> 00:07:15,815
It has the largest Japanese population outside Japan, and the coffee wealth of
the 1800s built its railways first and its industry later.

42
00:07:16,476 --> 00:07:23,430
Remember the coffee lines that became factories, and the state that holds the
biggest city in the southern hemisphere.

43
00:07:24,168 --> 00:07:26,084
Let's bring Paraná into view.

44
00:07:34,875 --> 00:07:48,006
Paraná lies in the south, on the Atlantic below São Paulo, with Curitiba, its
largest city, in the middle and Santa Catarina to its south and Mato Grosso do
Sul to its west.

45
00:07:48,665 --> 00:07:58,475
The Iguaçu falls are on its border with Argentina, and the Itaipu dam just
upstream was the largest hydroelectric plant in the world until Three Gorges.

46
00:07:59,128 --> 00:08:07,011
Remember the great falls on the border with the giant dam above them, and the
capital that gave the world the bus lane.

47
00:08:07,689 --> 00:08:09,907
Let's bring Santa Catarina into view.

48
00:08:17,310 --> 00:08:29,512
Santa Catarina sits on the south coast between Paraná and Rio Grande do Sul,
with Florianópolis, its largest city, on an island just off the mainland and
the Atlantic along its shore.

49
00:08:30,175 --> 00:08:38,024
It was settled heavily by Germans and Italians in the 1800s, and Blumenau
holds the second-largest Oktoberfest in the world.

50
00:08:38,676 --> 00:08:49,253
Remember the state of German and Italian settlers, with snow falling in its
highlands most winters and the highest life expectancy in Brazil.

51
00:08:49,954 --> 00:08:52,508
Let's bring Rio Grande do Sul into view.

52
00:08:58,206 --> 00:09:11,894
Rio Grande do Sul is the southernmost state, below Santa Catarina, with Porto
Alegre, its largest city, on the lagoon and the Atlantic coast beyond, facing
Uruguay and Argentina.

53
00:09:12,557 --> 00:09:20,568
It declared itself an independent republic in the 1835 Ragamuffin War and held
out against Brazil for ten years.

54
00:09:21,231 --> 00:09:29,497
Remember the southern republic that fought Brazil for ten years, with the
gaúcho culture of the pampas shared with Uruguay and Argentina.

55
00:09:37,749 --> 00:10:01,437
13 regions of Brazil, one for each target of the map: Rondônia, Mato Grosso,
Bahia, Distrito Federal, Goiás, Minas Gerais, Espírito Santo, Mato Grosso do
Sul, Rio de Janeiro, São Paulo, Paraná, Santa Catarina and Rio Grande do Sul.

56
00:10:02,096 --> 00:10:12,115
Remember the shape of Brazil from the inside: the regions nest around each
other, and every name on the map belongs somewhere in this one country.
